---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";

const title = "AI Network Operations Platform (MCP) | landrycmd";
const description =
  "Case study of the AI Network Operations Platform (MCP): 28 MCP servers, about 573 tools, 44 agents, and 31 skills. A standalone page, separate from the firewall request review.";
---

<Layout title={title} description={description}>
  <article class="prose">
    <p class="kicker">// case study</p>
    <h1>AI Network Operations Platform (MCP)</h1>
    <p class="meta">Network operations · standalone case study</p>

    <p>
      This is the public account of the AI Network Operations Platform (MCP):
      custom MCP servers that let agents carry network-operations work that
      used to be done by hand. It is its own page. It is not a tab, a section,
      or a diagram inside the firewall rule request work.
    </p>

    <ul class="scale">
      <li><strong>28</strong> MCP servers</li>
      <li><strong>~573</strong> tools</li>
      <li><strong>44</strong> agents</li>
      <li><strong>31</strong> skills</li>
      <li><strong>23</strong> agents I authored</li>
    </ul>

    <figure class="platform-figure">
      <svg
        viewBox="0 0 640 160"
        role="img"
        aria-label="Diagram of the AI Network Operations Platform (MCP): 28 MCP servers connect to about 573 tools, which connect to 44 agents."
      >
        <title>AI Network Operations Platform (MCP)</title>
        <desc>
          A straight row of three nodes. 28 MCP servers lead to about 573
          tools, which lead to 44 agents.
        </desc>
        <line x1="168" y1="48" x2="250" y2="48" />
        <line x1="390" y1="48" x2="472" y2="48" />
        <g>
          <rect x="24" y="24" width="144" height="48" rx="8" />
          <text x="96" y="54">28 servers</text>
        </g>
        <g>
          <rect x="248" y="24" width="144" height="48" rx="8" />
          <text x="320" y="54">~573 tools</text>
        </g>
        <g>
          <rect x="472" y="24" width="144" height="48" rx="8" />
          <text x="544" y="54">44 agents</text>
        </g>
      </svg>
      <figcaption>
        AI Network Operations Platform (MCP): 28 MCP servers, about 573 tools,
        and 44 agents, drawn in a straight row.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>

    <h2>What it is</h2>
    <p>
      Custom MCP servers expose the systems engineers already use — telemetry,
      source of truth, ticketing, addressing, and change records — so agents
      can carry work that used to be done by hand. I authored 23 of the 44
      shipping agents, including the firewall review and design agents. The
      scale is 28 MCP servers, about 573 tools, 44 agents, and 31 skills.
    </p>
    <p>
      <a href="/lab/mcp-simulator/">Open the MCP hub →</a>
    </p>

    <h2>What this page is not</h2>
    <p>
      The firewall request review is a separate lab: backlog from 200 to about
      40, and review time from 30–60 minutes to 3–5 minutes. This page does
      not host that flow. Internal runbooks stay off this site.
    </p>
    <p>
      <a href="/lab/frr-review/">Open the firewall request review →</a>
      &nbsp;·&nbsp;
      <a href="/resume">Résumé →</a>
    </p>
  </article>
</Layout>

<style>
  .scale {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.75rem 1.5rem;
    margin: 1.5rem 0;
  }
  .scale li {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--text);
  }
  .scale strong {
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
    color: var(--accent);
  }
  .platform-figure {
    margin: 0 0 2rem;
  }
  .platform-figure svg {
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    display: block;
  }
  .platform-figure line {
    stroke: var(--accent);
    stroke-width: 1.5;
    opacity: 0.7;
  }
  .platform-figure rect {
    fill: var(--bg-elev);
    stroke: var(--border);
  }
  .platform-figure text {
    fill: var(--text);
    font-size: 14px;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    text-anchor: middle;
  }
  .platform-figure figcaption {
    color: var(--text-dim);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    margin-top: 0.5rem;
  }
</style>
